2026-10-15 03:21:09,450 DEBUG: Chroma query output: {'ids': [['sluPolicy_tailgating_15', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_14', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_17', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_3', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_18', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_13', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_16', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_4']], 'embeddings': None, 'documents': [['. A non-licensed vehicle not parked in an identified parking space cannot be parked on sidewalks, shall not be parked where it can cause damage to grass or landscape and must always yield to pedestrians. • For purpose of this policy, Ned McGehee Drive (Friendship Circle) from McClimans Hall to Dyson Hall is considered pedestrian during tailgating activities', '. Such vehicles should be used as a mode of transportation to the tailgating location and parked for the duration of the tailgating activity except when moving to and from campus. Non-licensed vehicles are not to be parked on sidewalks, shall not be parked where it can cause damage to grass or landscape and must always yield to pedestrians. • Non-licensed vehicles considered “street legal” may be operated on campus streets and can be parked in an identified parking space', '. • Ned McGehee will reopen to motor vehicles 30 minutes after kick off. • Parking is always prohibited in driveways, walkways, building exits, fire lanes or any place that would inhibit access of emergency vehicles. • Parking for RVs will be located on the west side of Dyson Hall and the overflow lot located on the North side of the practice field. Reservations • All reservations must be submitted through the Lion Spots website in order to request a spot', '. • Setting up, marking off, or holding a tailgate space in Friendship Circle without a tailgate prior approval from the Director for Athletics is prohibited. • Digging or any form of staking to secure tents is strictly prohibited without consent from the Director for the Physical Plant. • Amplified sound, including but not limited to radio station vans, live bands, DJs, televisions, sound systems, small battery-powered devices, is permitted with approval by the Director for Athletics', '. • Please note that signage will not be placed marking reservation spots. Fans are required to mark their own space for game day once approved. • Only the President of the student organization can request to reserve a green student organization tailgating spot. • Students/Fans who submit a request will receive a text message when their spot has been requested, approved or denied. • Students/Fans must request a spot for each individual game', '. Tents cannot be staked to the ground or anchored to buildings. Vehicles • Non-licensed vehicles are defined as a vehicle primarily used for the transportation of persons or cargo and generally recognizable as a passenger or utility type cart, vehicle, “off-road vehicle”, golf cart, club car, etc. Nonlicensed vehicles are permitted for tailgating but are not to be driven through pedestrian areas as otherwise identified in this policy', '. This area will be free from all moving vehicles including but not limited to cars, trucks, and non-licensed vehicles, with the exception of emergency and university vehicles. • Motor vehicles parked on Ned McGehee Drive after the closure will be subject to citation or towing at the owner’s expense. • All vehicles must yield to pedestrians at all times and adhere to all other street closures identified through signage, barricades, etc', '. All sound must be terminated at the start of the game. Noise amplification and music must be kept to a reasonable level. Only Clean Music/Radio Version may be played at tailgate. • Soliciting or selling goods/services will not be permitted on stadium grounds without prior approval from the university. • Except as may be specifically authorized by University Police, the operation of drones/unmanned aircraft systems on University property is prohibited']], 'uris': None, 'included': ['metadatas', 'documents', 'distances'], 'data': None, 'metadatas': 